This python notebook:
https://github.com/Valentina-Garcia/vg-assignments/blob/main/module17_starter/Practical_Application_3_Jupyter_notebook.ipynb

is for analyzing data related to the factors that identify a sales contact 
is likely to subscribe to a long-term deposit to reduce the number of contacts 
required. The data comes from this study:
http://localhost:8888/files/CRISP-DM-BANK.pdf.

In the jupyter notebook various different classification models are built 
and their accuracy is tracked in a table for comparison. The data is 
split into a train and test set. Many of the models performed similarly 
wehn looking at the test set. A logistic regression model and a SVC classifier
using default parameters performed very well. 

The code requires pandas, numpy, matplot lib and seaborn along with python 3. 

#In the future the buisness can use the logistic regression pipeline to predict if someone is likely to sign up
#but if they don't have the pipeline for some reason, March is a very successful month for calls, the longer the call
#duration the more successful it is to be, and the price is very important for predicting if they will sign on.
